WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.640
It is Craft Week here at the show

2
00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:07.640
and I am so excited to get my DIY on with our next guest.

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.360
He's an environmental lifestyle expert.

4
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.360
Really kind of first to the party, a true pioneer.

5
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.250
And his magazine, "Naturally, Danny Seo"

6
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.060
is jam packed with amazing tips and tricks.

7
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.110
I've actually read this issue front to back.

8
00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:27.849
Please. welcome the original Danny Seo!

9
00:00:27.849 --> 00:00:29.730
(audience applauding)

10
00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:30.800
Hi, Drew.

11
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.610
That does look like a worn issue.

12
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.339
I got to get you a fresh one.

13
00:00:34.339 --> 00:00:36.340
Well, I mean it, though.

14
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.810
You were really first to the party with all of this

15
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:41.500
and everybody has sort of,

16
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.350
I'm happy to say jumped on a bandwagon

17
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:47.070
to be more environmentally conscientious.

18
00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.060
But you were doing it way before it was invoked.

19
00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:56.032
I think it's now gonna be 30 years.

20
00:00:56.032 --> 00:00:57.610
What are we gonna do today?

21
00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:01.420
We're gonna dye common cotton things, paper things,

22
00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.750
using this beautiful pink dye.

23
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:05.430
And can you guess what our one-ingredient

24
00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.240
natural source will be?

25
00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.033
Danny, tell us.

26
00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:10.250
I mean, it's kind of obvious,

27
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.670
there's a bowl of avocados right here.

28
00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.890
But we're using avocado pits.

29
00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.080
I love that.

30
00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:19.310
I have a real association and affinity for avocados

31
00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:20.900
and their pits.

32
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.210
And I knew that about you.

33
00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:25.710
You did?
(audience laughing)

34
00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.300
Oops, ah, see how slippery they are?

35
00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.133
I'm gonna grab it.

36
00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:29.580
And as they say in "Pretty Woman",

37
00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:30.860
slippery little suckers.

38
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.140
They're very slippery little suckers

39
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.830
and that's the avocado oil, that's the flesh.

40
00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:35.763
So you have to clean them really well.

41
00:01:35.763 --> 00:01:36.830
So dry them.

42
00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:37.900
So we're gonna dry them

43
00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.030 line:15%
but you want to get all that oil off.

44
00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:41.520 line:15%
So you get them really wet,

45
00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.900 line:15%
and what you can do is take a little bit of just,

46
00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.540 line:15%
we have a little shot of soap.

47
00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:48.410
You can take a little bit of soap

48
00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:50.810
and just get it off because the avocado oil

49
00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.180
all that's on the outside of the seed,

50
00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:54.610
that can actually get onto whenever you're dyeing

51
00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:56.060
and you don't want oil stains.

52
00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.510
And what we have in the bowl here, we have about,

53
00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:01.250
you need about six to eight avocado seeds

54
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.090
and you want them all to be clean.

55
00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:06.290
You put them into a pot of water.

56
00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:07.430
And then what you do

57
00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:10.290
is that you simmer this for about 45 minutes.

58
00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:11.360
Wait a minute.

59
00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.110 line:15%
Danny, this coloration is not from an avocado.

60
00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:16.607 line:15%
It is.
No!

61
00:02:16.607 --> 00:02:19.090 line:15%
Yes, you don't get a green dye,

62
00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.140 line:15%
you don't get a brown dye.

63
00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.855 line:15%
You get this beautiful pink dye from the seed.

64
00:02:22.855 --> 00:02:24.450 line:15%
You have got to be kidding me.

65
00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.470
I thought we were actually working with

66
00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:28.010
some type of color dye,

67
00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:30.460
and I was like, "Oh, I love Rose color."

68
00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:31.730
This is it.

69
00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:34.780 line:15%
This color is from the inside of the avocado?

70
00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.073 line:15%
Six avocado seeds and that's all you need.

71
00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.150
Okay--

72
00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:39.983
Easy.

73
00:02:39.983 --> 00:02:42.710
So what we're gonna do is simmer this for about 45 minutes.

74
00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:43.543
And then while we're doing that

75
00:02:43.543 --> 00:02:46.040
you want to get your materials you want to dye ready.

76
00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.900
I mean, this truly looks

77
00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.737
like one of those stores you walk in and you're like

78
00:02:49.737 --> 00:02:50.887
"Everything's so beautiful,

79
00:02:50.887 --> 00:02:53.540
"but how much is it gonna cost," because it's so chic.

80
00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.891
It kind of reminds me of that store

81
00:02:54.891 --> 00:02:55.724
ABC.
ABC.

82
00:02:55.724 --> 00:02:58.490
(audience laughing)

83
00:02:58.490 --> 00:02:59.594
We like the same things--

84
00:02:59.594 --> 00:03:02.610
I want to high five but I can't.

85
00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.007
So I see the pits and the color and everything,

86
00:03:05.007 --> 00:03:07.450
but I want to know exactly how to do this.

87
00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.210
You know, I'm not a pro pro at this,

88
00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.160
but what I do know is

89
00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.240
you want to fold whatever you're tie dyeing,

90
00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.250
sort of as many ways that you want, twist it around.

91
00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.640
But I just fold it a couple of times

92
00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.020
and take the rubber bands,

93
00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:20.160
and then you tightly

94
00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.340
just wrap the rubber bands around and around.

95
00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:25.670
So then after 45 minutes you want to let the dye cool down.

96
00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:27.940
So you don't burn your fingers.

97
00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.550
So it's not like boiling over,

98
00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:32.840
and you just put it in the dye like this.

99
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.390 line:15%
And then what I like to do, Drew,

100
00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:37.530 line:15%
is that I actually let it soak overnight.

101
00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:42.530
But I also find that I let it sit out for a day or two

102
00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:45.230
and then I wash it in cold water.

103
00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.480
That's perfect.
Oh good!

104
00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:47.480
Yeah, that's perfect--

105
00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:48.540
I'm doing it right?

106
00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.160
So we have a bowl of cold water here.

107
00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:53.220
You're gonna take the one that's been cooking,

108
00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.000
and the one that's already in there,

109
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.589 line:15%
and we're just gonna rinse it out.

110
00:03:57.589 --> 00:03:59.399 line:15%
And then we get to do the fun part.

111
00:03:59.399 --> 00:04:01.169 line:15%
Get to do the reveal!

112
00:04:01.169 --> 00:04:03.240 line:15%
What you could do if you want to be really, really eco

113
00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.870 line:15%
is actually take them off and reuse the rubber bands.

114
00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.530
Okay, goodness, I failed the first one.

115
00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.130
I will succeed on the second.

116
00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:13.010
Ready?

117
00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.230
One, two, three.

118
00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:19.000
Oh wow.
(audience applauding)

119
00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.060
Danny, this is gorgeous,

120
00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:23.583
and I have to tell you,

121
00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:28.770 line:15%
you can't really get this color in the dye world.

122
00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:30.680 line:15%
This is so unique.

123
00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:31.513 line:15%
You know what?

124
00:04:31.513 --> 00:04:33.690 line:15%
There's also a study that says that pupils dilate

125
00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:38.290
when you see something that you associate with pleasure.

126
00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:42.930
So guess what?
(audience laughing)

127
00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:44.963
My pupils are like (makes weird noise).

128
00:04:44.963 --> 00:04:46.350
(audience laughing)

129
00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:49.287
Danny, this is so beautiful.

130
00:04:49.287 --> 00:04:53.510
You can dry it and stuff it with a fresh pillow.

131
00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:54.920
And I should point out

132
00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.290
the tutorial for this avocado dyeing project

133
00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:00.101
is in the winter issue which comes out in December 6th.

134
00:05:00.101 --> 00:05:02.684 line:15%
(upbeat music)

